---
import CarpeItDoc from '../../layouts/CarpeItDoc.astro';
import { carpeitOperator } from '../../data/carpeitOperator';

const lastUpdated = '14 October 2026';
const email = carpeitOperator.email;
const a11yMail = `mailto:${email}?subject=${encodeURIComponent('CarpeIt accessibility')}`;
---

<CarpeItDoc
  title="CarpeIt — Accessibility"
  description="CarpeIt's accessibility statement: the standard we aim for, known gaps, and how to tell us about a barrier."
  heading="Accessibility"
  lastUpdated={lastUpdated}
>
  <p class="doc-lead">
    CarpeIt should work for everyone who wants to get on the water. This statement covers the
    CarpeIt apps for iPhone and Android and these CarpeIt web pages.
  </p>

  <h2>What we aim for</h2>
  <p>
    We aim to meet the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.1 at level AA, the standard
    referenced by the European accessibility standard EN 301 549. That includes working towards:
  </p>
  <ul class="doc-list">
    <li>Screens labelled for VoiceOver and TalkBack, with images and controls described.</li>
    <li>Text that scales with your system text size (Dynamic Type and Android font size).</li>
    <li>Colour contrast that meets AA, and information that never relies on colour alone.</li>
    <li>Animations that respect Reduce Motion and the equivalent Android setting.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Known gaps</h2>
  <ul class="doc-list">
    <li>The apps and these pages are currently available in English only.</li>
    <li>We have tested with accessibility tools and simulators, and a full review with VoiceOver and TalkBack on physical devices is ongoing. Some screens may still have unlabelled controls or awkward reading order.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Tell us about a barrier</h2>
  <p>
    If something in CarpeIt is hard or impossible for you to use, email
    <a href={a11yMail}>{email}</a> with the screen or page and what happened. We usually reply
    within 2 working days, and we'll do what we can to help you in the meantime.
  </p>

  <p class="doc-note">
    This statement was prepared on 14 October 2026, before CarpeIt's public launch, and will be
    reviewed after launch and at least once a year.
  </p>
</CarpeItDoc>
